Quick Stats, 2025 survey, acres harvested (data/reference/quickstats_2025_judges.csv)"},"benchmark":{"calibrated":{"silage":{"error":15743.0,"relative_error":0.393575},"grain":{"error":-23575.0,"relative_error":-0.0575}},"raw":{"silage":{"error":50433.0,"relative_error":1.260825},"grain":{"error":-58264.0,"relative_error":-0.14210731707317073}}},"method":"Maryland 2025 corn fields are Crop Sequence Boundaries polygons with at least half of their 2025 Cropland Data Layer pixels in corn: 18,684 fields, 442,169 acres. A seeded random sample of 1,500 fields, allocated by county, was read from Sentinel-2 L2A (July-November 2025) with the baseline's cloud mask and reflectance offset, giving nine NDVI features and four harvest-timing features per field. Model v2 (L1 logistic regression), fitted on all 44 labeled BARC field-years, gives each field a silage probability. Raw: probability-weighted silage acres in the sample, scaled to all Maryland corn acres. Calibrated: the acre share called silage, corrected with the miss and false-alarm rates measured on held-out BARC fields. Grain is corn acres minus silage. The 2025 NASS values were not used to fit, choose or adjust anything.","limitations":["The model was trained on 44 field-years from one research farm (BARC, 2021-2023); how well it transfers to other Maryland farms and to 2025 is untested.","The calibration rates come from 12 silage and 32 grain BARC field-years, so the calibrated range is wide.","The raw range reflects only which fields were sampled, not model error, so it is too narrow.","Field polygons date from 2023; corn in 2025 is taken from the Cropland Data Layer, which has its own classification error.","Corn acres here are mapped field acres, not NASS acres harvested; abandoned or failed corn is not removed.","Fields with fewer than 3 clear Sentinel-2 dates are skipped and listed, not filled in.","The timing feature drop_size is the largest NDVI fall between consecutive clear looks, so it grows with the gap between looks. BARC fields share scenes and cloud gaps; the statewide sample does not. Days between clear looks: 2025 sample median 5, 90th percentile 15, median longest gap per field 23; BARC training median 5, 90th percentile 15, median longest gap 29.","Model v2 was chosen on BARC held-out data (selection-corrected balanced accuracy about 0.87 vs 0.80 for v1; the bootstrap interval for the gain touches zero); its timing features are untested outside BARC."],"look_gaps_days":{"sample_2025":{"field_years":1500,"median_gap_days":5.0,"p90_gap_days":15.0,"median_longest_gap_days":23.0},"barc_training":{"field_years":44,"median_gap_days":5.0,"p90_gap_days":15.0,"median_longest_gap_days":29.0}},"sources":[{"name":"USDA NASS Crop Sequence Boundaries (fiboa copy on Source Cooperative)","url":"https://data.source.coop/fiboa/us-usda-cropland/us_usda_cropland.parquet","accessed":"2026-11-14"},{"name":"USDA NASS Cropland Data Layer 2025, Maryland (CropScape)","url":"https://nassgeodata.gmu.edu/webservice/nass_data_cache/byfips/CDL_2025_24.tif","accessed":"2026-11-14"},{"name":"Sentinel-2 L2A, Microsoft Planetary Computer STAC","url":"https://planetarycomputer.microsoft.com/api/stac/v1","accessed":"2026-11-14"},{"name":"BARC silage and grain corn labels 2021-2023 (repository GeoPackage)","url":"BARC_Corn.2021-2023.gpkg","accessed":"2026-11-14"},{"name":"USDA NASS Quick Stats 2025, corn acres harvested (judges' reference)","url":"https://quickstats.nass.usda.gov/","accessed":"2026-11-14"}]},"benchmark":{"label":"Per-row errors and descriptive summaries only. This is not a contest score: the judges' scored geographies and formula are unconfirmed.","unit":"ACRES HARVESTED","error_definitions":{"signed_error":"prediction - reference, in acres","absolute_error":"|prediction - reference|, in acres","relative_error":"(prediction - reference) / reference; null when the reference is 0"},"matching":"year, geography kind (NATIONAL, STATE, OTHER STATES), geography name and crop use; kinds 